\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar rises but trades in thin ranges.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Gertrude Chavez  \par \uc2 664 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Juni 2004\par 23:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK, June 22 (Reuters) - The dollar firmed but traded in narrow ranges on Tuesday as a weaker-than-expected German investor sentiment survey fueled a modest sell-off in the euro and other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 One trader cited a large order for dollars against the yen from a major fund as the engine for part of the dollar's gains, but some analysts said such transactions are fairly common in a market that has no direction.  \par \par \uc2 "I think people have backed away from the \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  market," said Steven Englander, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist for North America at Barclays Capital in New York.  \par \par \uc2 "For instance, the euro/dollar's 200-day moving average has been breached 14 times this year. That's clearly not a sign of a trending market. What this suggests is that there is a lot of uncertainty about the medium-term direction of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market," he added.  \par \par \uc2 In late New York trade, the euro was down about 0.1 percent at $1.2098 . Against the Swiss franc, the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  climbed to 1.2503 francs . Sterling fell 0.7 percent to $1.8191 .  \par \par \uc2 Against the yen, the dollar was up 0.35 percent at 109.25 yen . The euro also rose to 132.23 yen .  \par \par \uc2 Traders said the yen's sell-off in New York trading was also ostensibly triggered by rumors that Japan "may be getting upset at how fast the yen is rising." This followed earlier warnings from the Japanese finance ministry that it is still monitoring the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, even though \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  since mid-March.  \par \par \uc2 "In these types of markets which are in wait-and-see mode, that was just a small pop (in dollar/yen)," said Tim Mazanec, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist with Investors Bank & Trust in Boston.  \par \par \uc2 "We are definitely in a deep waiting period as the range keeps on narrowing each and every day," Mazanec said.  \par \par \uc2 UPBEAT JAPANESE OUTLOOK  \par \par \uc2 The yen had firmed earlier against major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as dealers continued to bet upcoming Japanese data would confirm a rosier economic outlook.  \par \par \uc2 Yen bulls remain optimistic that Japanese service sector data on Thursday and the Tankan corporate sentiment survey next week would encourage further inflows into the country's stock market.  \par \par \uc2 The euro declined earlier in the global day after the closely watched German ZEW institute investor confidence index posted its first rise of the year in June, improving to 47.4 points from 46.4 in May. The index, however, came in slightly below a Reuters analyst poll forecast of 48.  \par \par \uc2 Markets remain fixated on what it sees as a likely quarter percentage point rate hike by the Federal Reserve next week and the potential for larger rate moves later in the year. A rate hike is generally perceived as bullish for the dollar as it would enhance the appeal of U.S. assets to foreign investors.  \par \par \uc2 Foremost on traders' minds remains next week's Fed meeting, and analysts are all but certain the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will raise rates by a quarter percentage point. What happens at the Fed's meeting in August is less clear, and some expect a more aggressive half-point hike at that time.  \par \par \uc2 With markets fully pricing in a Fed tightening, there was little surprise that Fed speakers on Tuesday failed to move the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. Philadelphia Federal Reserve Bank President Anthony Santomero said the U.S. economy is strong, but over time it is likely to face a shortage of skilled workers as the job market changes.  \par \par \uc2 Federal Reserve Board Governor Donald Kohn also spoke on Tuesday but said nothing about the U.S. economic or monetary outlook.  \par \par \uc2 Federal Reserve Board Governor Susan Bies, on the other hand, said U.S. rates are too low and must be above inflation, but her comments had muted impact on the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by John Parry in New York and Kyle Peterson in Chicago).   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040622e06m0038u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
