\par\par \b \uc2 DJ.  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  MOF: Didn't  \highlight22\uc2 Intervene \highlight\uc2  In  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Market In May  \b0\par\par\uc2 308 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Mai 2004\par 22:04\par \uc2 OsterDowJones Commodity Wire\par \uc2 OSTDJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2004, Comtex News Network.  All Rights Reserved.  Standard Attribution Statement: News Provided by COMTEX.  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, May 31, 2004 (ODC via COMTEX) --  \par \par \uc2 Japan stayed out of the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets for the second straight month in May, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Monday, reporting no yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the period April 28-May 27. The zero \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which had been expected by market participants, confirms that revived market demand for dollars - rather than the heavy hand of Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities - kept the yen at depressed levels during the month. In April and May the dollar rebounded 11% from four-year lows against the yen even as Japan ended an aggressive campaign to keep its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weak. The dollar hit a peak of Y114.89 on May 14; at 1001 GMT Monday it was changing hands at Y109.89, partly pressured by the recent surge in oil prices. Fearing a sharp yen rise could derail the country's economic recovery by hurting exports, Tokyo sold more than Y15 trillion in the first three months of this year, an amount three-quarters the record \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  total for all of 2003. While the government has never explained its subsequent change of course - it maintains that its basic stance on \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  hasn't changed - analysts say the combination of an increasingly robust economy and pressure from the U.S. and other trading partners likely prompted the end of its heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Still, with the dollar's broad-based rally apparently running out of steam, many market participants say they expect the MOF to resume selling yen, albeit on a smaller scale, if the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  again moves sharply higher. Monday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  data covered settlement dates during May. \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trades are settled after two business days.  \par \par \uc2 -By Jonathan Soble, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; jonathan.soble@dowjones.com -Edited by Hugh Lawson  \par \par \uc2 Dokument OSTDJ00020040531e05v0030g\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
