\par\par \b \uc2 US Treasury Taylor:  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  Flexibility Is Our Principle  \b0\par\par\uc2 565 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Mai 2004\par 05:28\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--A senior U.S. treasury official said Thursday that the key principle of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  as far as the Group of Seven is concerned is flexibility, and that talks with Japan on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy have been consistent with G7 statements.  \par \par \uc2 U.S. Treasury Under Secretary for International Affairs John Taylor also said that the U.S. doesn't spend much time discussing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as long as the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is in line with G7 principles. [ 13-05-04 0348GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 "The discussions that we've had about financial and exchange markets over the months (with Japan) have been very consistent with the statements that are put out publicly by the G7," he told a press conference.  \par \par \uc2 The statements "call for flexibility in exchange markets," he said, noting that he raised this concern to Chinese officials earlier this week.  \par \par \uc2 "The particular action on a particular day, as long as they are consistent with that guiding principle, is not something we spend a lot of time discussing," Taylor said when asked about whether he had any indications in his talks that Tokyo had abandoned its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  campaign.  \par \par \uc2 Data released Wednesday by the Japanese Finance Ministry underlined two points: record \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the three months through March and a sudden halt to action after March 16 and into April.  \par \par \uc2 Japan sold Y14.83 trillion in the January-March quarter to stem a fall in the dollar and weaken the yen But foreign reserves fell $11.61 billion on month to $815.0 billion in April after big rises in the first three months of the year.  \par \par \uc2 Much of Japan's reserves are put into foreign securities, namely U.S. Treasurys, which some say is a factor helping keep U.S. interest rates down.  \par \par \uc2 Taylor, asked about the impact on U.S. rates from a stop to \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  buying of Treasurys because of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  halt, said that "\b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  portfolio decisions with regard to foreign reserves" aren't a big factor on rates. Some determinants include expectations for growth and inflation in the U.S. and other countries, he added.  \par \par \uc2 "I've always stressed that the United States' bond markets are very broad, strong and resilient. There are many people supplying and demanding in those markets," he said. "The decisions about portfolios are not a factor that would come into play as a major issue in analyzing those markets."  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. official is visiting Japan Wednesday through Friday as part of a one-week tour of Asia, which included a stopover in China on Monday and Tuesday and will be concluded with a visit to South Korea, starting Friday, to attend the annual meetings of the Asian Development Bank. During his visit to Tokyo, Taylor met with Finance Minister Sadazaku Tanigaki, banking minister Heizo Takenaka and Bank of Japan Governor Toshihiko Fukui.  \par \par \uc2 Taylor, questioned about a possible Chinese economic slowdown's impact on Japan, said that China recognizes inflationary pressures and is taking action to control them.  \par \par \uc2 "If those actions slow the Japanese economy down, I believe that it will by a a relatively small amount and should not have an impact of any major degree in Japan or elsewhere," he said.  \par \par \uc2 -By James Simms, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; james.simms@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by John Gibson and Bennett Richardson [ 13-05-04 0520GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040513e05d00043\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
