\par\par \b \uc2 DJ. BOJ Fukui: To Send Policy Messages To Mkts As Needed -2-  \b0\par\par\uc2 192 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Mai 2004\par 22:04\par \uc2 OsterDowJones Commodity Wire\par \uc2 OSTDJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2004, Comtex News Network.  All Rights Reserved.  Standard Attribution Statement: News Provided by COMTEX.  \par \par \uc2 May 13, 2004 (ODC via COMTEX) --  \par \par \uc2 Fukui said the status of government finances among developed nations has worsened in recent years, which inevitably has pushed up yields on government bonds. But he played down any suggestion that inflation risks, which can also hurt government bonds, would arise quickly in Japan or globally. Specifically on Japan, Fukui said the government has already started a policy that aims to improve its finances and achieve a primary balance by the 2010s. Asked about the impact of rising long-term interest rates in the U.S., Fukui said the rise "caused worries in Japan, but currently Japanese long-term rates are moving separately from those in the United States." The BOJ will aim to stabilize interest-rate expectations in \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , he added. On \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Fukui reiterated that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets isn't part of the BOJ's monetary policy. In Japan, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy is set by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 -By Asako Tanabe, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; asako.tanabe@dowjones.com -Edited by Kirsty Mackenzie and John Gibson  \par \par \uc2 Dokument OSTDJ00020040513e05d001p5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
