\par\par \b \uc2 Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Japan Stk Rise Drives Yen Higher Vs Dlr, Euro  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Leika Kihara  \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \uc2 704 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Mai 2004\par 07:47\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The yen rose against the dollar and the euro in Asia Wednesday, buoyed by Japanese exporters' bids and solid gains in Japanese stocks.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar-buying hype triggered by expectations of higher U.S. interest rates in early summer cooled after the greenback's overnight failure to climb past Y114 discouraged dollar bulls, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 The strong performance of Tokyo stocks supported the yen by making yen-denominated assets more attractive. Non-Japanese speculators covered short-yen positions after the Nikkei 225 Stock Average opened higher and extended gains throughout the day.  \par \par \uc2 Many Japanese exporters, who have been taking a wait-and-see stance, also came in with dollar offers when the U.S. unit slipped below Y113 early in the day, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar's weakness against the yen weighed on the euro/yen, sending the pair down by around one full yen to as low as Y133.28.  \par \par \uc2 Some market players believe it may take some time for the dollar to climb well above Y113. But the greenback's downside was firmly supported by dip-buying interest around Y112.50.  \par \par \uc2 Takeshi Iba, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi, expects the dollar to resume its uptrend after its short-term correction against the yen runs its course.  \par \par \uc2 "It's basically a strong-dollar market now," as economic fundamentals and prospects of a U.S. interest rate hike ahead still warrant a higher dollar, Iba said. He added there was still room for the greenback to test Y115 soon.  \par \par \uc2 At 0515 GMT, the dollar was quoted at Y112.65, below Y113.22 late Tuesday in New York. The dollar was at Y113.50 late Tuesday in Tokyo.  \par \par \uc2 The euro was at $1.1874, higher than $1.1864 late Tuesday in New York. The euro was at $1.1860 in Tokyo Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 Against the yen, the euro was quoted at Y133.80, down from Y134.36 in New York late Tuesday. The euro was at Y134.56 in Tokyo late Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 Sterling was at $1.7612, up from $1.7543 in New York but lower than $1.7754 in Tokyo Tuesday. [ 12-05-04 0547GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 The Nikkei 225 extended gains toward the close, finishing up 2.3% at 11153.58.  \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, data released by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  showed Japan spent a hefty Y14.83 trillion in the January-March quarter to prevent the yen from rising sharply against the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 More importantly, the data showed \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  abruptly ended its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  campaign on March 16, in line with many traders' expectations.  \par \par \uc2 Data released earlier in the month showed \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  didn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market in April. Many market players also believe no \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been carried out so far in May.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts say Wednesday's data strongly suggest U.S. criticism of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's heavy-handed \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was largely behind the MOF's decision to pull out of the market.  \par \par \uc2 Yasunari Ueno, chief market economist at Mizuho Securities, points out that the size of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  shrank notably after March 8, the day when U.S. Treasury Secretary John Snow obliquely criticized Japan's heavy yen-selling campaign.  \par \par \uc2 On March 8, Snow said relative value of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are best set through open and competitive \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. He added that "no \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  can be considered strong if it is propped up on life support with \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."  \par \par \uc2 "Snow also issued a warning against \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on March 17, and the day before that was the last day the MOF acted in the market," Ueno said.  \par \par \uc2 On March 17, Snow said: "Nobody can devalue their way to prosperity."  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    -By Leika Kihara, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; leika.kihara@dowjones.com \par    -Edited by Alastair Gale \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The chart of late Tokyo \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rates that accompanied Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been replaced with an enhanced \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fixture that is updated hourly.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Subscribers can find this table:  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -On Telerate pages 4046 and 1087.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -On Dow Jones Newswires by searching the code N/IFX  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -On Reuters by entering FRX or INT  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -On Bloomberg by entering NI FRX [ 12-05-04 0706GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1074  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040512e05c00089\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
