\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE:  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  Ended  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  In Mar After Record Sum  \b0\par\par\uc2 By James Simms and Iain McDonald  \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \uc2 824 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Mai 2004\par 07:18\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  abruptly ended its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  campaign on March 16 after a record-breaking stretch of dollar-buying, allowing the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to fall to a four-year low in the following two weeks, according to data issued Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  took action on 47 out of 64 trading days during the first two and a half months of the year, before stopping its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and apparently altering its strategy.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold Y14.83 trillion in the January-March quarter to stem a fall in the dollar and to weaken the yen when the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  eventually rebounded from mid-February onward.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to push the dollar higher when it was already rising in the second half of February and into March generated concern and, at times, criticism inside and outside Japan.  \par \par \uc2 Both Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan and U.S. Treasury Secretary John Snow directly commented on the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in early March.  \par \par \uc2 But an official of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Tokyo's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  actions were in line with a Group of Seven statement made by finance ministers and central bankers in Boca Raton, Florida in February.  \par \par \uc2 "Our principle stance on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy is shared by the G7. Our actions are in line with the G7 Boca Raton statement," the official told a news conference Wednesday. "We closely watch economic and market conditions when taking measures."  \par \par \uc2 G7 central bankers and finance ministers in their Boca Raton statement warned against "excess volatility and disorderly movements" in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par      MOF's Strategy Change May Not Last \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 When asked about \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from mid-February onward, the official said the action wasn't taken to set a certain yen level or to aggressively weaken the yen.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from mid-February through mid-March helped push the dollar up from a low of Y105.16 set Feb. 11 to Y112.34 on March 8.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Once the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervenes\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on MOF's orders, stopped entering the market, the dollar fell to a fresh four-year low of Y103.40 on March 31.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 For the whole fiscal year through March, the MOF spent Y32.87 trillion in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the largest amount for any fiscal year on record.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Another official said the first-quarter amount was the largest since the ministry began issuing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  data in April 1991.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  data are in line with traders' suspicions that \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has ended its aggressive \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  campaign.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 But it isn't clear if MOF's strategy has changed permanently, said analysts at Westpac Banking Corp.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Westpac noted that Tokyo didn't need to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in late March and April because capital flows data showed sizable net outflows of funds by Japanese investors buying foreign bonds.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Once the typical post fiscal-year-end period of Japanese foreign bond buying slows, and assuming the MOF remains absent from the market, a firmer conclusion may be able to be drawn," Westpac added.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 At 0518 GMT, the dollar was quoted at Y112.65.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par      Japan's Foreign Reserves Fall From Record High \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Wednesday's data also showed that \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  focused its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  campaign exclusively on the dollar.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 That isn't too surprising given that any purchases of euros to weaken the yen against the European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would have drawn criticism, particularly from the Europeans who were vocal in saying they didn't want to bear the brunt of a weaker dollar.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MOF also said Japan's foreign reserves fell $11.61 billion on month in April to $815.00 billion after big rises in the first three months of the year, in a further indication that Tokyo has ended its dollar-buying \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The fall follows March's jump of $49.72 billion from a month earlier to a record $826.58 billion of convertible foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , gold and International Monetary Fund special drawing rights.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The drop in April was due to the euro's decline against the dollar and falls in prices of foreign securities, according to a MOF official. Japan usually buys U.S. Treasurys and European government bonds with the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  it receives through \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 April's fall ended seven straight months of rises to record highs.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's reserves were the highest in the world for the 53rd straight month in February, the ministry said, citing data issued by the International Monetary Fund.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The IMF figures, which differ slightly from those issued by the MOF due to differences in gold evaluation methods, showed Japan had $768.3 billion in reserves as of February - far outstripping China, which was in second place with $426.4 billion as of November.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By James Simms and Iain McDonald, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; james.simms@dowjones.com, iain.mcdonald@dowjones.com  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Kirsty Mackenzie [ 12-05-04 0518GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040512e05c00072\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
