\par\par \b \uc2 Tsy's Taylor: Flexibility Is Guiding  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Principle  \b0\par\par\uc2 By James Simms  \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \uc2 923 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Mai 2004\par 14:42\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Senior U.S. Treasury official John Taylor said Wednesday that he has discussed \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  flexibility with various nations, including Japan and China, and that he is beginning to see some changes in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies.  \par \par \uc2 Partly because of a robust economic rebound, Tokyo also appears to have abandoned its massive campaign to weaken the yen against the dollar for now. And Beijing's long-stated goal is to eventually establish a more market-oriented \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  system and is continuing talks with Washington toward this end.  \par \par \uc2 "I just visited China as well. There our focus, along with China, is finding ways for them to move to a more flexible exchange rate, and so that's been basically our principle," the Treasury undersecretary for international affairs said.  \par \par \uc2 "And we discussed this with Japan and other countries and I think right now you're seeing some changes in policies and the good performance that results from that," he told Dow Jones Newswires and CNBC Asia Pacific in an interview.  \par \par \uc2 Indeed, data released Wednesday by the Japanese Finance Ministry underlined two points: record \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the three months through March and a sudden stop in action after March 16 and into April.  \par \par \uc2 That halt allowed the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to fall to a four-year low in the following two weeks. The MOF took action on 47 out of 64 trading days during the first two-and-a-half months of the year, before stopping its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and apparently altering its strategy.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold Y14.83 trillion in the January-March quarter to stem a fall in the dollar and to weaken the yen when the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  eventually rebounded from mid-February onward.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to push the dollar higher when it was already rising in the second half of February and into March generated concern and, at times, criticism inside and outside Japan. Both Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan and U.S. Treasury Secretary John Snow directly commented on the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in early March.  \par \par \uc2 But a Japanese MOF official said Tokyo's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  actions were in line with a Group of Seven statement made by finance ministers and central bankers in Boca Raton, Fla., in February.  \par \par \uc2 For his part, Taylor, asked about the MOF's herculean effort, as evidenced by the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  data, said that the U.S. guiding principle was flexibility, as seen in G7 statements.  \par \par \uc2 "The message that I would emphasize is the message that has been put in the G7 communique the last couple of times calls for more flexibility in exchange rates and that is our guiding principle," he said. "How that actually gets operated depends on the circumstances."  \par \par \uc2 But he also said that Tokyo's overall \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy was "exactly consistent with the G7."  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. official is visiting Japan Wednesday to Friday as part of a one-week tour of Asia, which included a stopover in China on Monday and Tuesday and will be concluded with a visit to South Korea, starting Friday, to attend the annual meetings of the Asian Development Bank.  \par \par \uc2 In China Tuesday, Taylor said no agreement has been reached within the nation on the type of flexible \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime to be pursued. China has a managed float that keeps the yuan's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate effectively pegged to the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 The yuan, or renminbi, is fully convertible only on the trade account and even then is kept in a tight band of around 8.2777 to the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 CNBC will broadcast portions of the interview Thursday. [ 05-12-04 1008ET ]  \par \par \uc2 With economic indicators showing signs of improvement, Tokyo's mandarins apparently believe the nation's exports and corporate balance sheets can weather a stronger yen.  \par \par \uc2 Indeed, the economy grew at a blistering real annualized pace of 6.4% in the three months through December, and economists' expect January-March gross domestic product, due out May 18, will top 3.0%.  \par \par \uc2 Taylor was also optimistic on Japan's economic outlook, but said that the nation needed to ensure there is balance among all sectors. Growth isn't just dependent on exports and includes "considerable" investment, improving consumption and the right monetary and bank reform policies.  \par \par \uc2 "For all reasons, this is a more sustainable situation than we've seen in a long time," he said. "If it's going to be sustainable you have to have balance in all the compositions of spending."  \par \par \uc2 Taylor also said that the deflation situation is also starting to improve because of the more aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , saying that the policies are "just right."  \par \par \uc2 "The policies that underlie the growth are different from the past: the good focus on monetary policy to try to end the deflation, which has been a drag on the Japanese economy. It's beginning to end. It reached its bottom and is coming back up again," he said.  \par \par \uc2 Recovering domestic activity has eased deflationary pressure, but consumer prices continue to fall slightly, reinforcing expectations the Bank of Japan will keep its zero-rate policy in place for some time.  \par \par \uc2 Japan's nationwide core consumer prices fell 0.1% in March from a year earlier. The BOJ uses nationwide core consumer prices as its chief price indicator and has pledged to keep its quantitative easing until year-to-year changes in nationwide core consumer prices stabilize at or above zero.  \par \par \uc2 -By James Simms, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; james.simms@dowjones.com [ 05-12-04 1106ET ]  \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020040512e05c0001n\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
