\par \par \uc2 Ahead of Friday's U.S. consumer price report, analysts looking to gauge price pressures will be checking producer price data, due on Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 Other key reports scheduled for Thursday include data on April U.S. retail sales and first-time jobless claims.  \par \par \uc2 In New York afternoon trading, the euro was at $1.1895, up about 0.17 percent. If the euro were to close above $1.1950, that could pave the way for a move up to about $1.2150, some traders said.  \par \par \uc2 Against the yen , the dollar was trading at 113.14 yen, up about 0.12 percent.  \par \par \uc2 Against the Swiss franc , the dollar was down about 0.21 percent at 1.2943 francs.  \par \par \uc2 Sterling was up 0.77 percent at $1.7717, partly on signals of future U.K. interest rate hikes.  \par \par \uc2 "I think the main focus of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market remains interest rates and Federal Reserve policy more than the trade balance," said Larry Brickman, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Banc of America in New York.  \par \par \uc2 Earlier on Wednesday, the dollar held steady against the euro and yen but stayed off recent peaks as rising Tokyo stocks lifted the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and a Fed official's comments tempered U.S. rate hike enthusiasm.  \par \par \uc2 On Wednesday morning, Chicago Fed President Michael Moskow reminded markets that the pace of U.S. monetary tightening this year is likely to be gradual and will depend on employment growth and inflation, just as Philadelphia Fed President Anthony Santomero did on Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 Santomero's comments also kept upcoming U.S. inflation data in focus, while the yen found support from the Nikkei stock average's biggest one-day gain this year.  \par \par \uc2 Government data on Wednesday showed \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Finance Ministry had refrained from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market since mid-March.  \par \par \uc2 Earlier, Bank of Japan policy board member Shin Nakahara said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would keep rates at zero even after ending its quantitative easing.  \par \par \uc2 The New Zealand dollar rose more than 1 percent against the greenback, receiving help from strong employment data that painted a robust picture of the domestic economy.  \par \par \uc2 Other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  managed to recover from recent falls against the dollar that had come on worries that attempts to cool China's economy could hurt the wider Asia-Pacific region.  \par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by John Parry in New York).   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040512e05c0031y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
