\par\par \b \uc2 No  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  MOF  \highlight22\uc2 FX Intervention \highlight\uc2  In April  \b0\par\par\uc2 265 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 April 2004\par 12:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The Japanese government did not conduct any yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in April, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Friday, providing evidence the government has ended its strategy of massive, all-out \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  aimed at underpinning the economy.  \par \par \uc2 The lack of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  comes in stark comparison to the record Y7.155 trillion sold in January, when the MOF was struggling to support the sagging dollar.  \par \par \uc2 The MOF also sold Y3.342 trillion in February and Y4.703 trillion in March.  \par \par \uc2 Government officials likely ceased their yen sales after judging that improvements in exports and production have also filtered through to other parts of the economy, making it better equipped at handling pressure from a more expensive \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . A strong yen makes Japanese products less competitive overseas, which hurts exports, and also reduces the yen-denominated value of exporters' overseas earnings.  \par \par \uc2 Despite the lack of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in April, the dollar has managed to rebound from a four-year low of Y103.40 marked March 31, as the strengthening U.S. economy boosts market hopes for an early hike in U.S. interest rates. The dollar, which hit a one-month high of Y111.04 on Thursday, was trading around Y110.20 at 1006 GMT.  \par \par \uc2 The April data cover transactions settled during the month, or \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  carried out between March 30 and April 27. \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trades are settled after two business days.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par   -By Miyako Takebe, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; miyako.takebe@dowjones.com   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Kirsty Mackenzie [ 30-04-04 1007GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040430e04u000js\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
