\par\par \b \uc2 Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Dollar Up Vs Yen On Faith In U.S. Economy -2-  \b0\par\par\uc2 420 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 April 2004\par 08:56\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 Given the rising expectations for U.S. interest rate rises, combined with likely growth in April U.S. non-manufacturing data next week, Tohru Sasaki, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at JPMorgan Chase Bank, said he has upgraded his dollar/yen outlook for the calendar year.  \par \par \uc2 Sasaki now expects the dollar to be trading at Y108 in early June, Y102 in early September and Y98 in early December. That compares to his previous forecasts for the dollar to be trading at Y102 in June, Y97 in September and Y95 in December.  \par \par \uc2 But others doubt dollar-buying on U.S. interest rate expectations alone will continue uninterrupted for long.  \par \par \uc2 "The rate hike expectations are still just speculation, and haven't even begun to affect the U.S. bond markets yet," said Noriyuki Fujita, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at Societe Generale in Tokyo. The U.S. interest rate outlook may lose its appeal as a dollar-positive factor, as history has proven that "dollar-bullish factors don't tend to last for too long," says Fujita.  \par \par \uc2 Separately, Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  is set to release to the total amount it spent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets in April later Friday.  \par \par \uc2 While traders say the figure will likely be more than zero, given that authorities were suspected of having been in the market on several occasions during the month, it's still likely to be much smaller than the Y4.7 trillion the MOF spent in March.  \par \par \uc2 A sharp fall in the government's yen-selling will effectively provide evidence the MOF has ended its all-out campaign to weaken the yen - a 15-month effort through March which resulted in an unprecedented Y35 trillion in yen sales, of which Y15 trillion was spent in the first three months of this year.  \par \par \uc2 The MOF, which \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  through the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , sold Y7.2 trillion in January, Y3.3 trillion in February and Y4.7 trillion in March.  \par \par \uc2 -By Miyako Takebe, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; miyako.takebe@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Alastair Gale and John Gibson  \par \par \uc2 The chart of late Singapore \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates that accompanied Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been replaced with an enhanced \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixture that is updated hourly.  \par \par \uc2 Subscribers can find this table:  \par \par \uc2 -On Telerate pages 4046 and 1087.  \par \par \uc2 -On Dow Jones Newswires by searching the code N/IFX  \par \par \uc2 -On Reuters by entering FRX or INT  \par \par \uc2 -On Bloomberg by entering NI FRX [ 30-04-04 0656GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040430e04u000be\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
