\par\par \b \uc2 Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Dollar Up Vs Yen On Faith In U.S. Economy  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Miyako Takebe  \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \uc2 921 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 April 2004\par 07:52\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The dollar advanced against the yen in Asia Friday, supported by lingering expectations of an early U.S. interest rate hike and general faith in the strength of the U.S. economy, despite initial disappointment over weaker-than-expected economic growth data.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. Commerce Department said Thursday gross domestic product expanded at an annual rate of 4.2% in the first quarter. That fell below expectations of economists surveyed by Dow Jones Newswires, who had forecast 5% growth, and prompted dollar-selling during overnight trade.  \par \par \uc2 But the price index of GDP, the broadest available measure of inflation, advanced at a 2.5% annual rate, keeping alive expectations for an early U.S. rate hike and supporting the dollar in Tokyo, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 "While faith in the strength of the U.S. economy prevails, it's unlikely there'll be a significant shift," out of dollars, a senior trader at a Japanese brokerage said.  \par \par \uc2 The yen was also hurt by weakness in Tokyo share prices, which took a hit on concerns that efforts by Chinese regulators to chill economic growth may weigh negatively on Asian equity markets and the Japanese economy.  \par \par \uc2 News that China's banking regulator ordered commercial banks to halt lending ahead of a week-long national holiday in May was said by some market players to have been the catalyst behind the yen's brief tumble to a one-month low of Y111.04 against the dollar overnight.  \par \par \uc2 While the yen later recovered on the dollar's weakness following the U.S. GDP data, it faced renewed selling against the dollar and the euro Friday in Tokyo after the Nikkei 225 Stock Average lost 2.9% at the open and prompted non-Japanese model funds to sell, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 "The China news - rather than having a direct impact on \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  - is likely hurting the yen through concerns that slower growth in China would negatively affect Asian stock markets and fears it may spell slower export growth for Japan," the trader at the Japanese brokerage said.  \par \par \uc2 "Still, most agree that Beijing will likely aim for a soft landing," keeping any impact limited, the trader said.  \par \par \uc2 At 0515 GMT, the dollar was quoted at Y110.12, down from a high of Y110.39 but still above Y109.76 late Thursday in New York. The dollar was at Y110.26 late Thursday in Singapore. Tokyo markets were closed Thursday for a national holiday.  \par \par \uc2 The euro was at $1.1971, a tad lower than $1.1978 late Thursday in New York. The euro was at $1.1833 in Singapore Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 Against the yen, the euro was quoted at Y131.78, down from a session high of Y132.10, but above Y131.54 in New York late Thursday. The euro was at Y130.46 in Singapore late Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 Sterling was at $1.7738, down from $1.7746 in New York but higher than $1.7699 in Singapore Thursday. [ 30-04-04 0552GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Given the rising expectations for U.S. interest rate rises, combined with likely growth in April U.S. non-manufacturing data next week, Tohru Sasaki, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at JPMorgan Chase Bank, said he has upgraded his dollar/yen outlook for the calendar year.  \par \par \uc2 Sasaki now expects the dollar to be trading at Y108 in early June, Y102 in early September and Y98 in early December. That compares to his previous forecasts for the dollar to be trading at Y102 in June, Y97 in September and Y95 in December.  \par \par \uc2 But others doubt dollar-buying on U.S. interest rate expectations alone will continue uninterrupted for long.  \par \par \uc2 "The rate hike expectations are still just speculation, and haven't even begun to affect the U.S. bond markets yet," said Noriyuki Fujita, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at Societe Generale in Tokyo. The U.S. interest rate outlook may lose its appeal as a dollar-positive factor, as history has proven that "dollar-bullish factors don't tend to last for too long," says Fujita.  \par \par \uc2 Separately, Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  is set to release to the total amount it spent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets in April later Friday.  \par \par \uc2 While traders say the figure will likely be more than zero, given that authorities were suspected of having been in the market on several occasions during the month, it's still likely to be much smaller than the Y4.7 trillion the MOF spent in March.  \par \par \uc2 A sharp fall in the government's yen-selling will effectively provide evidence the MOF has ended its all-out campaign to weaken the yen - a 15-month effort through March which resulted in an unprecedented Y35 trillion in yen sales, of which Y15 trillion was spent in the first three months of this year.  \par \par \uc2 The MOF, which \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  through the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , sold Y7.2 trillion in January, Y3.3 trillion in February and Y4.7 trillion in March.  \par \par \uc2 -By Miyako Takebe, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; miyako.takebe@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Alastair Gale and John Gibson  \par \par \uc2 The chart of late Singapore \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates that accompanied Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been replaced with an enhanced \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixture that is updated hourly.  \par \par \uc2 Subscribers can find this table:  \par \par \uc2 -On Telerate pages 4046 and 1087.  \par \par \uc2 -On Dow Jones Newswires by searching the code N/IFX  \par \par \uc2 -On Reuters by entering FRX or INT  \par \par \uc2 -On Bloomberg by entering NI FRX [ 30-04-04 0656GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 1074  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040430e04u0007h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
