\par\par \b \uc2 Japan Tanigaki: Didn't Discuss Japan  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  Policy With Snow  \b0\par\par\uc2 335 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 April 2004\par 03:13\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Japanese Finance Minister Sadakazu Tanigaki said Tuesday that Tokyo's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  wasn't discussed in a meeting he had with U.S. Treasury Secretary John Snow over the weekend.  \par \par \uc2 "Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  (policy) was not an issue," Tanigaki told a Parliamentary committee, when asked about his meeting with Snow in Washington Saturday.  \par \par \uc2 The bilateral meeting was held on the sidelines of the gathering of the Group of Seven finance ministers and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governors.  \par \par \uc2 Tanigaki also said that G7 officials generally shared the view that recent \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market movements appeared calm. [ 27-04-04 0136GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Japan has spent an unprecedented Y35 trillion to weaken the yen through \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the 15 months through March. But Tokyo appears to since have halted its large-scale \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recovering economy has lessened the necessity to hold down the yen.  \par \par \uc2 Tanigaki said that U.S. Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan and Bank of Japan Governor Toshihiko Fukui were also present at the meeting he had with Snow.  \par \par \uc2 When asked whether U.S. officials had addressed the possibility that higher global and U.S. interest rates may be a risk for the world economy, Tanigaki said that such concerns were expressed as part of broader discussions on the world economy.  \par \par \uc2 "But overall, the view was that the (global economy) is recovering in a healthy fashion," Tanigaki said.  \par \par \uc2 Fukui, speaking before the same Parliamentary committee Tuesday, added that U.S. officials indicated that it was important to ensure that interest rates don't shoot out of control.  \par \par \uc2 "Sudden leaps in the financial market are always a risk to the underlying economy," Fukui said.  \par \par \uc2 "It was a common understanding (in the bilateral meeting) that care must be taken so that (interest rates) don't shoot up," Fukui said.  \par \par \uc2 -By Miyako Takebe, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; miyako.takebe@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by John Gibson [ 27-04-04 0219GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040427e04r0001f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
