\par\par \b \uc2 Dollar bounce raises doubts on Japan  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  stance.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By David McMahon  \par \uc2 762 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 April 2004\par 06:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, April 22 (Reuters) - Just as \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  takes its foot off the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  pedal, the dollar has started climbing against the yen - in the very direction that trillions of yen of market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  had failed to carry it.  \par \par \uc2 Bolstered by upbeat U.S. economic data and a seasonal shopping spree by Japanese investors for foreign bonds, the dollar shot as high as 109.77 yen on Wednesday, more than six percent above four-year lows around 103.40 hit late last month. On Thursday it was around 109.34 yen  \par \par \uc2 While an apparent scaling back in \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , meaning removal of support, initially prompted the dollar's fall to those troughs, its ability to bounce against the yen despite a lack of help from Japanese authorities raises questions about the wisdom of Tokyo's large-scale market forays since last year.  \par \par \uc2 Some analysts say it may even be because of the absence of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  that the market's attention is returning to economic fundamentals, which are pointing to higher interest rates in the United States and therefore favouring the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 "The market focus has shifted from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  back to U.S. fundamentals," said Toru Umemoto, a research associate at the Global Security Research Centre of Tokyo's Keio University, headed by former \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF) official Eisuke Sakakibara.  \par \par \uc2 "We've already seen an exit from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and for now I think there's only a small chance we'll see it renewed."  \par \par \uc2 The MOF sold some 35 trillion yen ($322.7 billion) in the 15 months to March in an attempt to halt the yen's rise against the dollar and protect Japan's export-led economic recovery.  \par \par \uc2 Defenders of the policy say \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  helped slow the pace of the yen's rise against the dollar, but critics argue that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , by distorting supply and demand, only delays the market finding a natural bottom.  \par \par \uc2 "In the end you get a repetition of periods of yen strength followed by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," former MOF official Toyoo Gyoten said in a recent interview with business weekly Toyo Keizai.  \par \par \uc2 "Just because you help push the dollar to 112 yen from 105 through \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the market isn't going to settle there because everybody knows this movement isn't reflecting the market's free will."  \par \par \uc2 The dollar climbed to just above 112 yen in early March - helped by MOF \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said - but weeks later had erased all its gains and tumbled to the four-year low of 103.40.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  OVERRATED?  \par \par \uc2 Some analysts say the ability of authorities to influence the global \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market - which has a daily turnover of over $1 trillion - is overrated.  \par \par \uc2 "People have a kind of misconception that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  can influence the market to a great extent," said Eishi Wakabayashi, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist and president of Wakabayashi \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  Associates.  \par \par \uc2 "If markets really want to go down they will go down even if there is huge \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . If they want to go up, whether or not there is \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has nothing to do with it," said Wakabayashi, who accurately predicted the dollar's fall to an all-time low of around 80 yen in 1995.  \par \par \uc2 Recent Group of Seven (G7) meetings have featured veiled criticism of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and calls for flexible \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies, but at a G7 meeting this Friday and Saturday in Washington \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are not expected to be a major talking point.  \par \par \uc2 Many analysts are not ready to say \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy has ended, but say strong data on the Japanese economy is giving the MOF confidence to take its foot off the pedal.  \par \par \uc2 "Japanese authorities in the last couple of weeks seem to be more accepting of the fact that Japanese economic fundamentals have improved, and that an improvement in fundamentals is consistent with some strengthening of the yen," said Robert Rennie, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Westpac in Sydney.  \par \par \uc2 Some analysts say a fall in the dollar below 100 yen would likely trigger a revival of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and that the benefits of this policy continue to outweigh the costs.  \par \par \uc2 "They've prevented a sharper fall in the yen that would have occurred, and that's allowed greater confidence to develop in asset prices and in the economy," said Paul Gibbs, a senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist in Asia for RBC Capital Markets.  \par \par \uc2 "I'm trying to think of what benefit there would have been in Japan letting the yen strengthen more than it did, and I can't really think of one."  \par \par \uc2 ($1=108.44 Yen).   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040422e04m000gd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
