\par\par \b \uc2 Japan Tanigaki: To Act In  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Mkt If Disorderly Moves  \b0\par\par\uc2 296 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 April 2004\par 06:50\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets if needed to curb sharp rises in the yen, Japanese Finance Minister Sadakazu Tanigaki said Thursday, stressing that Tokyo's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy hasn't changed despite a lack of aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in recent weeks.  \par \par \uc2 "It is necessary to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if exchange rates move excessively or in a disorderly manner," Tanigaki told Parliament. "We will take appropriate action when necessary." [ 22-04-04 0501GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 In response to questioning by an opposition lawmaker, Tanigaki defended Japan's aggressive campaign to curb the yen's rise, which saw the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  dump Y20 trillion into the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market last year and another Y15 trillion this year through March.  \par \par \uc2 Although it has never acknowledged a policy shift, the ministry in effect ended its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  drive in late March, allowing the dollar to fall to a four-year low and prompting speculation that Tokyo had backed off under pressure from the U.S.  \par \par \uc2 But Tanigaki said the U.S. had not objected to Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy and that Tokyo's fundamental stance remained unchanged.  \par \par \uc2 "Our policy is based on the consensus among G7 countries that exchange rates should move stably, in line with economic fundamentals," he said, repeating \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's long-standing policy line.  \par \par \uc2 Tanigaki said the massive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  effort had been necessary to counter "extreme speculation," which threatened to drive the dollar sharply lower on concerns about the U.S. current account and budget deficits and last year's war in Iraq.  \par \par \uc2 "There was no lack of necessity or rationality" in the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  drive, he said.  \par \par \uc2 -By Jonathan Soble, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; jonathan.soble@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Kirsty Mackenzie [ 22-04-04 0526GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040422e04m0004v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
