\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  Fukuda: \highlight22\uc2 FX Intervention \highlight\uc2  Not To Make Exports Cheaper  \b0\par\par\uc2 214 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 April 2004\par 09:10\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Nikkei/Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  campaign hasn't been aimed at making exports cheaper, the government's top spokesman said Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 Instead, it's been about ensuring the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market functions smoothly, Chief Cabinet Spokesman Yasuo Fukuda told a news conference.  \par \par \uc2 "We've been acting in order to prevent sudden \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate moves from harming the normal function of the market," Fukuda said.  \par \par \uc2 "It's not at all about cheapening exports," he said.  \par \par \uc2 Fukuda was asked about the impact of the government's yen-selling campaign on merchandise trade. Earlier in the day, the government said Japan's overall trade surplus expanded 16.3% to Y11.238 trillion last fiscal year. Exports hit a record Y56.634 trillion.  \par \par \uc2 Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  ordered more than Y15 trillion in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the first three months of this year - an amount already three-quarters the record \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  total for all of 2003.  \par \par \uc2 Market players say the authorities appear to have backed off from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  now that the dollar is now rebounding naturally from nearly four-year lows, finding support as U.S. economic data strengthen the view that the Federal Reserve will raise interest rates before long. [ 21-04-04 0815GMT ]  \par 