\par\par \b \uc2 Tanigaki -  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2 's  \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention \highlight\uc2  fights deflation.   \b0\par\par\uc2 353 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 April 2004\par 05:43\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, April 17 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's efforts to hold the yen down were aimed at fighting deflation and would be understood by Group of Seven officials, a newspaper on Saturday quoted Finance Minister Sadakazu Tanigaki as saying.   \par \par \uc2 The comments came ahead of a meeting of G7 finance ministers and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governors in Washington at the end of next week.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy has been a key issue at recent G7 meetings as the dollar tumbled against the euro and the yen and Japan sought to protect an export-led economic recovery.   \par \par \uc2 "It has meaning as a way to prevent excessive moves in the market and to get rid of deflation," Tanigaki told business daily Nihon Keizai Shimbun in an interview, referring to \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 Tanigaki said \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , "would be able to gain international understanding" at the forthcoming meeting of leading economic powers, Nihon Keizai reported.   \par \par \uc2 The U.S. Treasury Department, in a report released on Thursday, called Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets in the second half of 2003, estimated at $230 billion daily, "extremely large".   \par \par \uc2 But the U.S. report also said no major trading partner had manipulated its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to gain a trade advantage in that period.   \par \par \uc2 Tanigaki said \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's stepped up \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  efforts from around late last year were due to fears about deflation.   \par \par \uc2 "At that time, deflation was viewed more gravely than now, so we could not stand idly by while the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market underwent rapid swings in a short period of time," Tanigaki said.   \par \par \uc2 Besides posing a possible threat to Japan's export-led economic recovery, a firm yen could derail its efforts to halt a fall in consumer prices, although some believe a recent increase in commodity prices could limit the impact of a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rise.   \par \par \uc2 Japan has spent about 35 trillion yen ($323.5 billion) over the past 15 months to hold the yen down, but financial markets believe that Tokyo has scaled back its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since mid-March, giving the United States less reason to complain. ($1=108.19 Yen).    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040417e04h001md\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
