\par\par \b \uc2 SCHEDULE-Asia Business News at 0515 GMT.   \b0\par\par\uc2 792 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 April 2004\par 07:16\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     Editor: Anne Marie Roantree\par     Telephone: 65 6870 3852\par     All times GMT.\par     TOP STORIES:\par     SEOUL - Samsung posts record profit, makes bullish forecast\par     BANGALORE - Wipro profit rises, sees steady growth\par     TOKYO - Nomura set for $462 mln takeover of Japan retailer\par     CANBERRA - EADS/Qantas awarded $1.5 bln aircraft deal\par     - - - -\par     COMPANIES SEOUL - Samsung Electronics Co Ltd, Asia's most\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2  valuable electronics company, says its quarterly profit almost    \par \par \uc2  trebles to a record on roaring demand for chips, handsets and    \par \par \uc2  flat screens, and forecasts a solid second quarter.    \par \par \uc2  (TECH-KOREA-SAMSUNG (UPDATE 3), moved at 0316, by Jean Yoon and    \par \par \uc2  Kim Miyoung, 880 words)    \par \par \uc2  BANGALORE - Wipro Ltd says its quarterly profit rose a    \par \par \uc2  better-than-expected 55 percent and forecast stable growth, as    \par \par \uc2  India's third-largest software services company benefits from    \par \par \uc2  overseas clients turning to cheaper outsourcing.    \par \par \uc2  (TECH-INDIA-WIPRO (UPDATE 2), expect by 0630, by Anshuman Daga,    \par \par \uc2  700 words)    \par \par \uc2  TOKYO - Nomura Holdings plans to inject around 50 billion    \par \par \uc2  yen to take over Seibu Department Store group as part of a 100    \par \par \uc2  billion rescue package for the struggling Japanese retailer,    \par \par \uc2  industry sources close to the deal say. (FINANCIAL-NOMURA-SEIBU    \par \par \uc2  (UPDATE 2), moved at 0432, by Emi Emoto, 650 words)    \par \par \uc2  SYDNEY - National Australia Bank Ltd warns first-half    \par \par \uc2  earnings will fall as much as 10 percent due to \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  movements and K pension costs, dismaying investors already    \par \par \uc2  reeling from rogue trading losses. (FINANCIAL-AUSTRALIA-NAB    \par \par \uc2  (UPDATE 2), moved at 0331, by Michael Smith, 600 words)    \par \par \uc2  CANBERRA - Australia awards a A$2 billion ($1.5 billion)    \par \par \uc2  contract for five air-to-air refuelling aircraft to European    \par \par \uc2  aerospace group EADS, hot on the heels of a similar contract    \par \par \uc2  from Britain. (ARMS-AUSTRALIA-REFUELLERS (UPDATE 2), expect by    \par \par \uc2  0630, by Belinda Goldsmith, 550 words)    \par \par \uc2  SEOUL - South Korea sells entire stake in Hana Bank for    \par \par \uc2  $928 million to unidentified buyers, wrapping up the    \par \par \uc2  privatisation of the country's fourth-biggest lender.    \par \par \uc2  (FINANCIAL-KOREA-HANA (UPDATE 2), expect by 0730, 500 words)    \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE - The Singapore Exchange has begun preliminary    \par \par \uc2  talks with Malaysia's Kuala Lumpur Stock Exchange on closer    \par \par \uc2  cooperation as ties between the two neighbours warm and    \par \par \uc2  Southeast Asia looks for ways to integrate financial markets.    \par \par \uc2  (FINANCIAL-SINGAPORE-EXCHANGE (UPDATE 2), expect by 0700, by    \par \par \uc2  Doreen Siow, 500 words)    \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG - Huaneng Power International, China's largest    \par \par \uc2  independent electricity producer, is set to announce the    \par \par \uc2  purchase of more generating assets from its state-owned parent,    \par \par \uc2  part of a deal-making frenzy amid booming China's power    \par \par \uc2  shortage. (ENERGY-HUANENGPOWER-SUSPENSION (UPDATE 2), moved at    \par \par \uc2  0450, by Daisy Ku and Tony Munroe, about 580 words)    \par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI - China Construction Bank, the country's top    \par \par \uc2  property lender, remains on track to float shares in a $5 to    \par \par \uc2  $10 billion global IPO by end-2004 at the earliest, its top    \par \par \uc2  executive tells Reuters, trouncing widespread reports of a    \par \par \uc2  delay. (FINANCIAL-CHINA-CONSTRUCTION (UPDATE 2, INTERVIEW),    \par \par \uc2  expect by 0700, by Ben Blanchard, about 600 words)    \par \par \uc2  TOKYO - Yoko Yamaguchi, a 33-year-old Japanese business    \par \par \uc2  administrator, spends nearly $200 on cosmetics each month;    \par \par \uc2  there are millions of other Japanese women just like her, one    \par \par \uc2  good reason why global cosmetics companies such as world leader    \par \par \uc2  L'Oreal want to colour Japan with a bigger foreign presence.    \par \par \uc2  (FASHION-JAPAN-COSMETICS (BUSINESS FEATURE), picture, moved at    \par \par \uc2  0132, by Yuka Obayashi, 950 words)    \par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI - The Bank of China, the nation's premier \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign    \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2  exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  bank, wants to slash its bad debt burden dramatically    \par \par \uc2  by the end of this year, as it prepares to float shares    \par \par \uc2  domestically or overseas. (FINANCIAL-CHINA-BANKOFCHINA (UPDATE    \par \par \uc2  1), moved at 0340, 316 words)    \par \par \uc2  - ~- --    \par \par \uc2  MARKETS/ECONOMY SEOUL - South Korea's unemployment rate    \par \par \uc2  edges up while payrolls fall in March from the previous month,    \par \par \uc2  highlighting the bumpy road ahead for a broad-based recovery in    \par \par \uc2  domestic consumption. (ECONOMY-KOREA-JOBS (UPDATE 2), expect by    \par \par \uc2  0700, by Yoo Choonsik, 600 words)    \par \par \uc2  BEIJING - China's latest quarter of blistering economic    \par \par \uc2  growth, fuelled largely by an investment boom, puts pressure on    \par \par \uc2  Beijing to take more drastic steps to cool the economy. But the    \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  rules out an interest rate hike in the near-term.    \par \par \uc2  (ECONOMY-CHINA, expect by 0600, by Scott Hillis, about 600    \par \par \uc2  words)    \par \par \uc2  TOKYO - With an economy running at its fastest pace in 13    \par \par \uc2  years and its controversial \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  apparently    \par \par \uc2  winding down, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be less defensive than usual at next    \par \par \uc2  week's Group of Seven meeting. (ECONOMY-JAPAN-G7, expect by    \par \par \uc2  0700, by Ritsuko Ando, 800 words)    \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE - Prices of everything from stocks to property in    \par \par \uc2  emerging economies are climbing and economists are concerned    \par \par \uc2  the huge pool of monetary stimulus could cause asset bubbles,    \par \par \uc2  but a reality check shows Asia is not headed for a catastrophe.    \par \par \uc2  (ECONOMY-ASIA-RISK (ANALYSIS), by Vidya Ranganathan, moved at    \par \par \uc2  0434, 800 words).    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040416e04g000l7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
