\par\par \b \uc2 Ex-MOF officials give mixed  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  reviews.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Ritsuko Ando  \par \uc2 773 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 April 2004\par 11:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, April 14 (Reuters) - As \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's top \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  official, Zembei Mizoguchi, appears to be winding down a long battle against the yen's surge, his predecessors offer a mixture of sympathy and criticism.  \par \par \uc2 The former officials agreed in separate interviews with Reuters over the past week that the government was scaling back its massive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, a change Mizoguchi and the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  have not officially acknowledged.  \par \par \uc2 Kosuke Nakahira, who held the same post of vice finance minister for international affairs from 1993 to 1995, gave the ministry credit for protecting \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's export-led economic recovery.  \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  helped to smooth rapid changes in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, and in that sense it led to a sustained recovery," Nakahira said.  \par \par \uc2 He also said the increasing amount of yen sold in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was in part inevitable because the market's overall volume had risen over the years.  \par \par \uc2 His inclination to sympathise with Mizoguchi and current ministry officials may be influenced by his experience of directing \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the yen shot to a record high of around 79.7 yen to the dollar in 1995.  \par \par \uc2 But Eisuke Sakakibara, who also oversaw massive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  during his 1997-99 term and is still known as "Mr Yen" for his influence in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, was more critical.  \par \par \uc2 He said he preferred \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  that was conducted over a short period of time but was large enough to deliver a clear message to the market.  \par \par \uc2 "\b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  shouldn't go on all the time," he said of the repeated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the past year, adding that the amount of yen being sold recently had been excessive.  \par \par \uc2 "It had always been very clear that the massive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would have to end," he said.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has sold about 35 trillion yen ($327.7 billion) in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market over the past 15 months to preserve strength in its exports. As a result, the country's foreign reserves ballooned to a record $826.577 billion in March.  \par \par \uc2 Makoto Utsumi, top \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  official from 1989 to 1991, also said would not have spent as much.  \par \par \uc2 "I would have found that kind of massive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  a bit too frightening," he said.  \par \par \uc2 "That said, there was some meaning in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the yen's rise, which threatened to nip an economic recovery in the bud."  \par \par \uc2 SCALED-BACK \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 But the three agreed that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  appeared to be scaling back its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , although there was a slight difference in views over whether it was a deliberate change in policy.  \par \par \uc2 While Sakakibara said Japan had adopted an "exit policy", both Nakahira and Utsumi said an increasingly stable \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market rather than a deliberate shift in policy had dictated the change.  \par \par \uc2 "Rather than saying \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has ended \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , I'd say the market's situation is such that it doesn't have to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  so much anymore," Nakahira said, predicting more \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the market became unstable again.  \par \par \uc2 Looking ahead, Utsumi said the government ought to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the yen sinks too low, a change he said would inevitably occur at some point in the long term.  \par \par \uc2 "\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy will come into question unless it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the yen falls excessively," he said. "Rather than only acting when the yen rises, they must show some symmetry in policy."  \par \par \uc2 The three officials also agreed \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  would not be a major topic at a meeting of Group of Seven (G7) finance minsters and central bankers due to be held in Washington around the end of next week.  \par \par \uc2 They also expected little change in the Washington meeting from a statement issued at the last G7 meeting in Boca Raton, Florida, in early February. That statement said excessive volatility in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates was undesirable but also called for exchange rate flexibility.  \par \par \uc2 The Boca Raton statement seemed to soothe market nerves after the group's previous statement, issued in Dubai, gave no warning on excessive volatility but called for flexibility.  \par \par \uc2 The Dubai statement triggered a surge in the yen as markets interpreted it as a criticism of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's massive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 "\b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  will probably not be an issue because current levels are comfortable for everyone," Sakakibara said. "I think it will be a meeting where everyone cheers a global economic recovery."  \par \par \uc2 Utsumi said he could not rule out a change in wording and there may be some mention of rising oil prices, but that the message on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  would likely remain the same.  \par \par \uc2 "It will likely warn against excessive volatility but again seek more policy flexibility from countries that aren't flexible," he said.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040414e04e0016i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
