\par\par \b \uc2 SCHEDULE-Asia Business News at 0505 GMT.   \b0\par\par\uc2 569 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 April 2004\par 07:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     Editor: Neil Fullick\par     Telephone: 65 6870 3852\par     All times GMT.\par     TOP STORIES:\par     SYDNEY - Telstra hammers out $250 million takeover of Kaz\par     TOKYO/SEOUL - Fujitsu files countersuit against Samsung SDI\par     TOKYO - Moody's raises rating on Japan government's foreign\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bonds\par     SYDNEY - \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  leaves rates unchanged again\par     - - - -\par     SYDNEY - Telstra Corp, Australia's biggest phone group,\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 says hammers out $250 million cash deal to buy technology   \f28 \par \par \uc2 services company Kaz Group. (TELECOMS-AUSTRALIA-TELSTRA (UPDATE   \par \par \uc2 2), moved 0243, by Sophie Hares, 630 words)   \par \par \uc2 - ~- --   \par \par \uc2 TOKYO/SEOUL - Fujitsu files countersuit against South   \par \par \uc2 Korea's Samsung SDI Co in a California court claiming patent   \par \par \uc2 infringements on plasma display panel technology, underscoring   \par \par \uc2 the intensifying competition in the electronics market.   \par \par \uc2 (TECH-FUJITSU-SAMSUNG (UPDATE 3), expect by 0700, by Daisuke   \par \par \uc2 Wakabayashi and Kim Miyoung, 600 words)   \par \par \uc2 - ~- --   \par \par \uc2 TOKYO - Rating agency Moody's raises its rating on Japan's   \par \par \uc2 foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  government bonds, but the market shrugs off   \par \par \uc2 the move, seen as overdue recognition of Japan's economic   \par \par \uc2 recovery; the more important domestic bond rating is left   \par \par \uc2 unchanged. (JAPAN-RATING-MOODY'S (UPDATE 2), expect by 0600, by   \par \par \uc2 David McMahon, 500 words)   \par \par \uc2 - ~- --   \par \par \uc2 SHANGHAI - The surprise departure of four top Lucent   \par \par \uc2 executives in China over suspected bribery shines a spotlight   \par \par \uc2 on the murky business landscape in the world's fastest-growing   \par \par \uc2 major economy. (TELECOMS-CHINA-LUCENT, expect by 0700, by   \par \par \uc2 Godwin Chellam, 600 words)   \par \par \uc2 - ~- --   \par \par \uc2 SYDNEY - Australia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  leaves interest rates   \par \par \uc2 unchanged for a fourth straight month after two rate rises late   \par \par \uc2 last year leads to slower retail sales and housing activity,   \par \par \uc2 suggesting a borrowing boom has cooled.   \par \par \uc2 (ECONOMY-AUSTRALIA-RATES (UPDATE 2), moved 0140, by Miranda   \par \par \uc2 Maxwell, 650 words)   \par \par \uc2 - ~- --   \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE - Japanese shares rise to fresh 32-month high   \par \par \uc2 while South Korea and Australia hit two-year peaks, but   \par \par \uc2 technology shares wobble, taking their cue from weak   \par \par \uc2 counterparts on Wall Street. (MARKETS-GLOBAL (WRAPUP 2), expect   \par \par \uc2 by 0730, by Neil Fullick, 700 words)   \par \par \uc2 - ~- --   \par \par \uc2 SEOUL - New data point to accelerating economic growth in   \par \par \uc2 South Korea, with foreign investment picking up, the service   \par \par \uc2 sector showing signs of recovery and a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  economist   \par \par \uc2 saying first quarter GDP growth likely to top forecasts.   \par \par \uc2 (ECONOMY-KOREA (WRAPUP 1), expect by 0700, by Yoo Choonsik, 600   \par \par \uc2 words)   \par \par \uc2 - ~- --   \par \par \uc2 TOKYO - Aeon Co Ltd, Asia's number two retail group, is   \par \par \uc2 expected to report healthy net profits for the year just ended   \par \par \uc2 as strong performances at its credit card and shopping mall   \par \par \uc2 development units more than offset weak clothing sales   \par \par \uc2 (RETAIL-JAPAN-AEON (UPDATE 2), expect by 0800, by Yuko Inoue,   \par \par \uc2 500 words)   \par \par \uc2 - ~- --   \par \par \uc2 TAIPEI - United Microelectronics Corp (UMC), the world's   \par \par \uc2 second-largest contract maker of semiconductors, reports March   \par \par \uc2 sales figures as plants running at full capacity churn out   \par \par \uc2 chips for wireless Internet applications and advanced   \par \par \uc2 cellphones. (TECH-TAIWAN-UMC (UPDATE 1), expect by 0700, by   \par \par \uc2 Kirby Chien, 400 words)   \par \par \uc2 - ~- --   \par \par \uc2 TOKYO - Japan's foreign reserves balloon to a record   \par \par \uc2 $826.577 billion in March after further Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but the pace of growth is likely to slow   \par \par \uc2 if, as widely believed, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has rowed back on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 (ECONOMY-\b \highlight22\uc2 JAPAN\b0 \highlight\uc2 -RESERVES (UPDATE 2), expect by 0700, by Mariko   \par \par \uc2 Hayashibara, 600 words)   \par \par \uc2 - ~- --   \par \par \uc2 TAIPEI - Taiwan reports its latest trade data. A Reuters   \par \par \uc2 poll of economists sees exports up 9.4 percent in the year   \par \par \uc2 through March on strong demand from China for raw materials and   \par \par \uc2 components. (ECONOMY-TAIWAN-TRADE (UPDATE 1), expect by 0900,   \par \par \uc2 by James Peng, 400 words)   \par \par \uc2 - ~- --.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040407e047000n2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
