\par\par \b \uc2 Japan March Foreign Reserves $826.58B; Up $49.72B On Mo  \b0\par\par\uc2 388 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 April 2004\par 01:50\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves rose $49.72 billion in March from a month earlier to a record $826.58 billion, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Wednesday, reflecting the government's continued yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  carried out during the month.  \par \par \uc2 The increase in \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's reserves of convertible foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , gold and International Monetary Fund special drawing rights comes after the MOF ordered the Bank of Japan to sell Y4.703 trillion in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in March to keep the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's appreciation in check.  \par \par \uc2 March's on-month rise in reserves - the seventh in a row - follows a $35.61 billion gain in February and a record $67.7 billion surge in January. The gains in reserves roughly correspond with the Y3 trillion in yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  MOF carried out in February, and the Y7 trillion conducted in January.  \par \par \uc2 But the pace of growth in reserves may slow in coming months, as traders believe the MOF has toned down its aggressive yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since mid-March, in line with improvements in the underlying Japanese economy. [ 06-04-04 2357GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 A ministry official briefing reporters on the data, said that March also marked the seventh straight month that Japan's reserves rose to a new record figure.  \par \par \uc2 According to MOF, the dollar's high for the month during Tokyo trading was Y112.30 marked March 8, while the low was Y103.75 on March 31. Its average for the month was Y108.62.  \par \par \uc2 Japan's reserves were also the highest in world for the 52nd consecutive month in January, the ministry said, citing comparable data issued by the IMF.  \par \par \uc2 The IMF figures, which differ slightly from those issued by MOF due to difference in gold evaluation methods, showed Japan had $732.6 billion in reserves as of January - far outstripping China, which was in second place with $426.4 billion as of November.  \par \par \uc2 The euro-area came in third, with $245.4 billion as of January. The euro area includes Austria, Belgium, Finland, France, Germany, Ireland, Italy, Luxembourg, the Netherlands, Portugal, Spain and Greece.  \par \par \uc2 -By Miyako Takebe, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; miyako.takebe@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by John Gibson and Bennett Richardson [ 07-04-04 0021GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 4146  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040406e046000x9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
