\par\par \b \uc2 Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Dlr Jumps Vs Yen, Prompting  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Talk  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Jonathan Soble  \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \uc2 849 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 April 2004\par 07:48\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The dollar surged against the yen in Asia Tuesday as buying by Japanese investors sparked a flurry of short covering by foreign hedge funds, prompting talk that Tokyo \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , acting through the Bank of Japan, may have fanned an initial rise in the dollar as a reminder to traders that it's still capable of swaying the market despite its apparent lack of action in recent weeks, some dealers speculated.  \par \par \uc2 But while "there's a lot of talk about the BOJ, no one's confirmed anything," said Satoshi Tate, a vice president for \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at UFJ Bank, which often acts as an agent for \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 He said buying by U.S.-based hedge funds to cover short positions was likely behind the acceleration in the dollar's rise.  \par \par \uc2 Other dealers agreed that any push from Tokyo was likely small, noting that the dollar quickly retreated from its high of Y107.20 after jumping more than a yen and a half. That suggested the MOF wasn't working actively to support the U.S. unit.  \par \par \uc2 A ministry official, speaking on condition of anonymity, declined to say whether the MOF had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but said there was no change to Tokyo's stance of fighting excessively sharp market moves.  \par \par \uc2 Traders said Japanese institutional investors were heavy buyers of both dollars and euros Tuesday as they adjusted their portfolios for the start of Japan's fiscal year, which began April 1.  \par \par \uc2 Some investors bought foreign stocks and bonds, but many were simply paring hedge positions on their existing holdings, a head dealer at a European brokerage in Tokyo said.  \par \par \uc2 "There's a lot of portfolio adjustment going on, and some life insurers and other institutional players are looking to take more risk on their foreign assets," he said.  \par \par \uc2 Investor buying pushed the dollar and the euro gradually higher against the yen through mid-afternoon trading, finally triggering heavy stop-loss sell orders, particularly in the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 At around 0515 GMT, the dollar was quoted at Y106.34, well above Y105.00 late Monday in New York. The dollar was at Y104.67 late Monday in Tokyo.  \par \par \uc2 The euro was at $1.1988, lower than $1.2013 late Monday in New York. The euro was at $1.2097 in Tokyo Monday.  \par \par \uc2 Against the yen, the euro was quoted at Y127.51, up from Y125.85 in New York late Monday. The euro was at Y126.63 in Tokyo late Monday.  \par \par \uc2 Sterling was at $1.8208, down slightly from $1.8217 in New York and lower than $1.8275 in Tokyo Monday. [ 06-04-04 0548GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Some Japanese insurance companies were said to be buying back hedge positions on their foreign assets.  \par \par \uc2 A Tokyo brokerage dealer noted that several firms are preparing to make the switch from mutual to joint-stock status. Most life insurers fully hedge their \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  risks, but the change may be prompting them "to take another look at their risk-return ratios," he said.  \par \par \uc2 Underlying the dollar's bullish tone was a string of positive U.S. economic data, starting late last week with the announcement that the U.S. economy created 308,000 new jobs March - the fastest rate of growth since April 2000 and well above market forecasts for a 120,000 gain.  \par \par \uc2 Then on Monday, the Institute for Supply Management said that its non-manufacturing index spiked to a record 65.8 in March from 60.8 in February, beating expectations for a reading of 61.4.  \par \par \uc2 Strong U.S. data have fueled buying of the dollar on expectations that the Federal Reserve may hike interest rates sooner than previously expected.  \par \par \uc2 In the days and weeks ahead, however, the overall impact on the dollar against the yen will likely be "neutral," said Minoru Shioiri, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at Mitsubishi Securities.  \par \par \uc2 Japan's economy is also showing signs of strength, he said, noting that recovery here is based largely on strong demand from the U.S. for Japanese exports - demand which would only be boosted by an acceleration in the U.S. rebound.  \par \par \uc2 The yen may still find itself under pressure in the coming weeks however. Some traders predicted Japanese institutional investors would continue to adjust their portfolios through the end of April, with related yen sales perhaps even accelerating toward the end of the month.  \par \par \uc2 "At the very least that's going to cap any further yen gains," a Japanese bank dealer said.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    -By Jonathan Soble, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; jonathan.soble@dowjones.com   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Alastair Gale  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The chart of late Tokyo \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rates that accompanied Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been replaced with an enhanced \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fixture that is updated hourly.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Subscribers can find this table:  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -On Telerate pages 4046 and 1087.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -On Dow Jones Newswires by searching the code N/IFX  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -On Reuters by entering FRX or INT  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -On Bloomberg by entering NI FRX [ 06-04-04 0639GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1074  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040406e0460006d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
