\par\par \b \uc2 Yen upbeat as tankan confirms Japan economy improving.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Mariko Hayashibara  \par \uc2 557 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 April 2004\par 05:21\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, April 1 (Reuters) - The yen was buoyant on Thursday, rising near a four-year peak against the dollar on a broad improvement in Japanese corporate sentiment.  \par \par \uc2 The closely watched quarterly "tankan" survey by the Bank of Japan (BOJ) showed that more Japanese firms felt they were doing better in March than at any time in nearly seven years.  \par \par \uc2 The main diffusion index for big manufacturers came in at plus 12, the highest since June 1997 and the fourth straight quarter of improvement.  \par \par \uc2 Yen bulls were heartened to see that brightening sentiment was also spreading to non-manufacturing and smaller firms, and many felt that \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  would not be a serious hurdle to pushing up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 "Japan's economic fundamentals are obviously good with the yen looking set to move towards the 100 per dollar level, brushing aside any yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Kouki Muroi, deputy manager at Aozora Bank's \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading group.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar slipped to a low of 103.85 yen after the suial year that started on Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 Large manufacturers forecast an average dollar rate of 108.43 yen in fiscal 2004/05, versus the current level around 104.40.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts said that given recent yen strength most companies must have revised down the level and were concerned how it affected their earnings outlook.  \par \par \uc2 The BOJ said roughly 40 percent of respondents submitted their results by March 9, when the dollar was at 111.21 yen and 90 percent of responses arrived by March 22, when the dollar closed at 106.97 yen.  \par \par \uc2 But many analysts said that Japanese companies are capable of enduring a strong yen.  \par \par \uc2 "In the second half of the previous financial year, most companies revised down the dollar/yen rate but revised up their earnings forecasts, suggesting they are much more resilient to a strong yen," said Junya Tanase, \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at JP Morgan Chase.  \par \par \uc2 "Japanese companies would have no problem with the dollar/yen at the 105 level, or even 100 to 95 level," he said.  \par \par \uc2 Azusa Kato, economist at BNP Paribas, held a similar view.  \par \par \uc2 "Three months ago, most people were expecting the yen's strength to dampen the manufacturing sector recovery, but the (tankan) figures show that the shipment volume increase thanks to strong global demand is supporting growth," she said.  \par \par \uc2 Such a view is underscored by foreign investors' persistence in pouring capital into Japan's assets.  \par \par \uc2 Latest data from the Finance Ministry on weekly capital flows suggests that net Japan stock purchases by foreigners from March 1 to March 26 totalled 2.58 trillion yen ($24.75 billion).  \par \par \uc2 The monthly volume would be the highest since the ministry started keeping data in March 1998, so long as foreigners did not sell stocks heavily in the remainingt 1330 GMT and keenly watched for a clue about Friday's important U.S. payrolls data.  \par \par \uc2 The market is also looking to the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's policy meeting. Its decision on interest rates is due at 1145 GMT, followed by a news conference with ECB President Jean-Claude Trichet at 1230 GMT.  \par \par \uc2 The common European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was at $1.2280 down from above $1.23 in late U.S. trade on caution over the ECB's rate decision. ($1=104.23 yen).   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040401e041000po\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
